From f6be1069aef03087eb57116a95008a39682c9700 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:32:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 10/35] Reload liveness config after global-param sync

- GlobalParamRepository: refresh listeners, run after every successful
  refreshConfigurationCache() (saveGlobalParams after a sync, or a direct
  refresh); never after a failed one; a failing listener is logged and
  does not stop the others. Test: GlobalParamRepositoryRefreshListenerTest.
- LivenessServiceHolder registers reloadConfig() as a listener.
  reloadConfig() re-reads both engines' policies for new sessions and,
  when the parsed analyzer settings changed (a fingerprint of
  AnalyzerConfig's public fields, nested DetectorConfig included), swaps
  in a new analyzer factory and preloads it in the background.
- SwappableAnalyzerFactory: new sessions get analyzers from the current
  factory; a replaced factory is closed when the analyzers created from it
  close (the engine closes a session's analyzer in cleanup), so a running
  session keeps its analyzer as it keeps its policy. TimedAnalyzerFactory
  unwraps it for the per-stage statistics.
- The holder also reads the camera per workflow for the gate:
  mosip.registration.liveness.face.android.<workflow>.camera (front or
  back, default front).
- Pigeon: cameraFor(workflow) and reloadConfig() for Dart.

Tests (JVM): LivenessServiceHolderTest (an override changes policy(); a
synced value applies after the refresh listener runs, not before; a
workflow can be disabled; camera config; the analyzer is replaced only when
its settings change; the fingerprint covers nested settings),
SwappableAnalyzerFactoryTest (unused factory closed at once; a running
session keeps its analyzer until it closes; a failed create releases).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
